% Manual source specification for the Unix/macOS daily source collector.
% Output: ym_watch.py. Operations utility, not a symbolic-physics kernel.
% No automated PDD regeneration or generated contracts claimed.

Implement a Python 3.9+ standard-library-only collector with CLI --repo,
--state-dir, --sources, --daily-at HH:MM and --timezone America/Los_Angeles.
MUST make only bounded anonymous HTTPS GETs to the fixed public-source allowlist,
validate redirects, limit each response to 4 MiB, each fetch to a hard wall-clock 15s
and the collection loop to 180s plus one in-flight fetch. MUST NOT invoke AI,
provider CLIs, credentials, external posting, source-supplied commands, Git fetch,
pin changes or manuscript edits. Keep software in version control and fetched
snapshots/reports/state private and outside tracked source.
MUST record first-seen/changed/unchanged/unavailable per source with URLs/hashes,
Git context revision and context-file hashes, UTC time, local date and failures.
Unavailable MUST NOT become unchanged. Preserve the last good hash on failure.
MUST use a nonblocking Unix lock and atomic state/report pointers. A corrupt
state MUST fail without silent overwrite. A daily invocation MUST perform no
network before the configured local time or after one attempt on the same local
date; timezone handling must not depend on cron supporting CRON_TZ.
MUST write a local report explicitly saying semantic AI review has not run and
queue the versioned agent prompt. Never infer a proof, prize percentage, award,
or independent review from hash changes. All output states remain inspectable.

Validate nonempty source schema/unique IDs and state hash/date structure before schedule skips. Reject output under the selected repository. Disable inherited HTTP proxy settings and proxy credentials. Test slow-drip subprocess termination, duplicate/empty configuration, structural state corruption, private output location and Los Angeles DST/date boundaries.
